    "fileId": 25606,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\">Subtypes of squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) of the oral cavity and mobile tongue</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Mark W. Lingen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.4pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"930\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">OSCC subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">References</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Acantholytic SCC</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Squamous carcinoma with acantholysis in epithelial islands creating a gland or duct-like appearance</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare in the oral cavity, may occur on the lip, has a poor prognosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{15045535; 21410819; 17071808; 25364162} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Adenosquamous carcinoma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Carcinoma with both squamous and adenocarcinoma components</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Aggressive and infiltrative behaviour, frequent metastases, associated with a worse prognosis than conventional OSCC</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26255977; 21305368; 10102394; 27456683} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Basaloid SCC</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Carcinoma with islands composed of basaloid cells, often with comedonecrosis and a high mitotic rate</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High-grade carcinoma, which often metastasizes, with overall survival similar to conventional OSCC</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{23946211; 25120708; 31912260} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Carcinoma cuniculatum</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Very well differentiated, lacking cytological malignancy, burrowing invasion pattern, keratin-containing crypts, abundant intraepithelial and stromal neutrophils</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Destructive bone invasion but no metastases</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22085046; 30607347; 25443811} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphoepithelial carcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Carcinoma with minimal differentiation and numerous interspersed non-neoplastic lymphocytes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">70% are associated with regional lymph node metastases, most are EBV-positive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{21698444; 33526225; 32462279} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Papillary SCC</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exophytic carcinoma with multiple thin, filiform, finger-like papillary projections; keratinizing and non-keratinizing types; cytological atypia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Better prognosis than conventional OSCC of a similar clinical stage, worse prognosis than verrucous carcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{22672806; 23797720} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Spindle cell SCC</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>(sarcomatoid carcinoma)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Carcinoma without epithelial tissue architecture and composed of spindle cells; may develop by transformation from conventional OSCC, often after radiotherapy</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Aggressive, recurs and metastasizes easily; oral cavity lesions have a worse outcome than do conventional OSCCs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{33982148; 24634155; 20730609} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 1.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 153.7pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"205\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Verrucous SCC</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 364.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"486\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Low-grade, surface carcinoma with verrucous architecture that lacks atypia and shows pushing cohesive invasion</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Good prognosis; an indolent, mostly laterally spreading carcinoma that carries a long-term risk of development of OSCC</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 179.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 1.0pt;\" width=\"239\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26156885; 22225903; 27924463} </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">OSCC, oral squamous cell carcinoma.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
